WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:03.920
I've still got a lot of years ahead of me

00:00.250 --> 00:03.920
Kono omoi wo keshiteshimau niwa

00:03.890 --> 00:05.810
To just erase these feelings?

00:03.890 --> 00:05.900
Mada jinsei nagai desho?

00:05.810 --> 00:05.850
To just erase these feelings?

00:05.850 --> 00:05.900
To just erase these feelings?

00:07.270 --> 00:08.900
I want to go back and finish

00:07.270 --> 00:08.900
Yarinokoshiteru koto

00:08.900 --> 00:12.530
The things that I've yet to finish.

00:08.900 --> 00:12.530
Yarinaoshite mitai kara

00:21.580 --> 00:28.790
I was supposed to be chasing after my ongoing dream,

00:21.580 --> 00:28.790
Yume no tsuzuki oikaketeita hazu nanoni

00:29.290 --> 00:35.130
Yet I faltered over others while walking this thin, winding path.

00:29.290 --> 00:35.130
Magarikunetta hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

00:35.130 --> 00:38.300
It's not that I want to return to those days.

00:35.130 --> 00:38.300
Ano koro mitainitte modoritai wake ja nai no

00:38.300 --> 00:41.810
I'm searching for the sky I lost.

00:38.300 --> 00:41.810
Nakushitekita sora wo sagashiteru

00:41.810 --> 00:43.480
Don't make that sad face, as if you've fallen victim.

00:41.810 --> 00:43.480
Wakatte kuremasu youni

00:43.480 --> 00:48.690
As if you want people to pity you.

00:43.480 --> 00:48.690
Gisei ni natta youna kanashii kao wa yameteyo

00:48.690 --> 00:50.400
Tears aren't the end of your sins.

00:48.690 --> 00:50.400
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo

00:50.400 --> 00:52.070
You have to bear them painfully, forever.

00:50.400 --> 00:52.070
Zutto kurushiku seottekunda

00:52.070 --> 00:53.740
Who are you waiting for in the maze of emotions,

00:52.070 --> 00:53.740
Deguchi mienai kanjoumeiro ni

00:53.740 --> 00:55.400
Where you can't even see the exit?

00:53.740 --> 00:55.400
Dare wo matteruno?

00:55.400 --> 00:57.200
I want to blurt it out more justly,

00:55.400 --> 00:57.200
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta youni

00:57.200 --> 00:58.950
Just like how I wrote it in my white notebook.

00:57.200 --> 00:58.950
Motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

00:58.950 --> 01:00.620
What do you want to run from?

00:58.950 --> 01:00.620
Nani kara nogaretainda

01:00.620 --> 01:02.240
That thing called "reality"?

01:00.620 --> 01:02.240
Genjitsu tte yatsu?

01:02.240 --> 01:05.580
I just want to scream out,

01:02.240 --> 01:05.580
Kanaeru tame ni ikiterundatte

01:05.580 --> 01:09.000
"I'm only living to fulfill my wish." Can you hear me?

01:05.580 --> 01:09.000
Sakebitaku naru yo kikoeteimasuka?

01:09.000 --> 01:13.130
I can't take the safe way out of everything.

01:09.000 --> 01:13.130
Bunan ni nante yatterarenaikara

01:14.090 --> 01:15.920
I don't even have a place to return to.

01:14.090 --> 01:15.920
Kaeru basho mo nai no

01:15.920 --> 01:19.220
I'm always thankful for everyone's kindness,

01:15.920 --> 01:19.220
Yasashisa ni wa itsumo kansha shiteru

01:19.220 --> 01:22.600
That's why I want to become stronger. (I'm on the way)

01:19.220 --> 01:22.600
Dakara tsuyoku naritai (I'm on the way)

01:22.600 --> 01:24.560
This is reminding me of the old days.

01:22.600 --> 01:24.560
Natsukashiku naru

01:24.560 --> 01:27.810
This pain is all right with me.

01:24.560 --> 01:27.810
Konna itami mo kangei jan

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
<b>One is All, All is One</b>

01:30.000 --> 01:33.000
<b>One is All, All is One</b>

01:46.160 --> 01:49.160
We're almost at Dublith, Brother.

01:50.990 --> 01:51.990
Were you dreaming?

01:52.830 --> 01:54.040
Yeah.

01:54.040 --> 01:55.500
A dream about him.

02:01.250 --> 02:03.840
We're finally here, aren't we?

02:03.840 --> 02:04.720
Yup.

02:05.800 --> 02:08.550
I hope the Master isn't home...

02:08.550 --> 02:09.430
Yeah...

02:20.230 --> 02:21.940
H-Hi...

02:21.940 --> 02:23.440
It's been a while...

02:24.030 --> 02:25.240
Welcome.

02:25.240 --> 02:26.820
You've gotten bigger.

02:26.820 --> 02:28.490
I-I'm going to shrink...

02:28.950 --> 02:31.450
Hi... It's me, Alphonse.

02:31.830 --> 02:33.330
It's been a while.

02:35.660 --> 02:37.920
You've really  gotten bigger.

02:38.540 --> 02:42.380
That's the first time I've been patted on the head since I became like this.

02:43.250 --> 02:46.340
Izumi, the Elric runts are here.

02:46.720 --> 02:47.970
Think you can get up?

02:48.340 --> 02:49.510
I'm fine.

02:49.510 --> 02:51.550
I'm not feeling too bad today.

02:52.050 --> 02:54.260
I guess she was lying down because she wasn't feeling well.

02:54.260 --> 02:56.560
Has her body not healed yet?

03:08.820 --> 03:11.200
You're one idiot of a disciple!

03:11.200 --> 03:13.580
What's this I hear about you becoming a dog of the military?!

03:20.120 --> 03:22.670
Master! W-Well... about this...

03:23.880 --> 03:27.170
Al! Look at how much you've grown!

03:29.930 --> 03:32.300
You haven't changed much either, Mast-

03:36.270 --> 03:37.890
You've slacked on your training!

03:37.890 --> 03:39.100
Oww...

03:39.100 --> 03:41.400
I thought you weren't feeling well?

03:41.400 --> 03:44.900
Forget about that! I'm out of bed like this because I heard you guys were here...

03:48.860 --> 03:50.400
Don't push yourself.

03:51.160 --> 03:54.700
You're worried about me, Dear?

03:59.290 --> 04:01.540
I don't know much about the Philosopher's Stone.

04:02.170 --> 04:03.790
Because I'm not interested.

04:03.790 --> 04:05.290
I see...

04:06.210 --> 04:10.670
We met an alchemist in Central who knew a lot about the stone, didn't we?

04:12.550 --> 04:13.640
What was he like?

04:13.970 --> 04:16.890
I think his name was...

04:17.560 --> 04:18.720
...Hohenheim.

04:29.320 --> 04:30.190
What's the matter?

04:31.280 --> 04:32.700
So he's alive...

04:33.200 --> 04:34.240
You know him?

04:35.620 --> 04:36.870
He's our father.

04:38.200 --> 04:39.870
So the one who left a long time ago...

04:40.330 --> 04:41.410
That bastard!

04:43.790 --> 04:46.670
It's his fault Mom died.

04:47.210 --> 04:48.750
Because of him...

04:54.130 --> 04:57.600
Oh! What are you doing up so early?

04:59.560 --> 05:01.810
Al said he needed to pee...

05:01.810 --> 05:03.980
Oh, so you were taking care of Al.

05:03.980 --> 05:05.810
Thank you, Ed.

05:31.920 --> 05:33.590
Mom, where's Dad?

05:37.640 --> 05:38.600
He left.

05:38.850 --> 05:40.510
When's he coming back?

05:44.520 --> 05:47.310
Tickle tickle tickle!

05:48.310 --> 05:49.730
Tickle tickle tickle!

05:50.360 --> 05:52.070
He'll be back in no time.

05:52.690 --> 05:54.190
Hurry and finish your meal, now.

05:58.370 --> 05:59.700
Mom...

06:01.580 --> 06:02.950
Mom.

06:04.870 --> 06:06.000
Mom!

06:13.420 --> 06:14.340
Mom!!!

06:26.850 --> 06:30.480
So... did Dad say anything about the stone?

06:31.060 --> 06:35.490
He looked happy, saying something about his wish from long ago will finally be coming true soon.

06:38.660 --> 06:39.490
Ow!

06:40.490 --> 06:41.620
Time to eat!

06:42.200 --> 06:43.830
Okay...

06:49.000 --> 06:50.380
You aren't going to eat, Al?

06:50.380 --> 06:51.880
N-No!

06:51.880 --> 06:54.250
I ate too much on the train...

06:54.250 --> 06:58.840
Hey Al, tell them about how we witnessed childbirth over at Rush Valley!

06:58.840 --> 07:00.010
Oh yeah!

07:00.010 --> 07:03.720
Master, we helped a baby being born!

07:03.720 --> 07:07.390
Idiot, that doesn't count as "helping".

07:08.310 --> 07:11.940
I learned that people are born because everyone in the family works together,

07:11.940 --> 07:15.480
the mother risks her life, and because the person receives so many blessings from everyone.

07:15.900 --> 07:16.990
That's right.

07:17.650 --> 07:20.240
That's how you two were given life, too.

07:20.240 --> 07:22.490
Be proud that you were born.

07:31.790 --> 07:32.880
Brother.

07:32.880 --> 07:33.790
Hm?

07:34.130 --> 07:35.750
Master hasn't changed at all, has she?

07:36.050 --> 07:37.300
Nope.

07:37.300 --> 07:39.510
She hasn't changed at all since we first met her.

07:52.270 --> 07:53.110
Hang in there!

07:53.110 --> 07:54.110
Bring over some more!

07:54.110 --> 07:55.440
It's going to collapse!

08:00.820 --> 08:03.620
The levee's going to break! Run for high ground!

08:04.240 --> 08:05.780
Brother, look!

08:09.960 --> 08:11.420
Hey, it's dangerous!

08:38.280 --> 08:40.070
This should last for a while.

08:41.400 --> 08:43.070
W-Who are you?

08:43.700 --> 08:45.740
A passing housewife!

08:52.210 --> 08:54.210
Will you please be our master, old lady?!

09:00.130 --> 09:01.880
Please, old lady!

09:01.880 --> 09:04.930
I couldn't catch exactly what you said...

09:05.340 --> 09:07.430
Mind repeating it?

09:08.470 --> 09:10.390
C-Correction!

09:10.390 --> 09:12.480
Please be our master, Miss!

09:12.480 --> 09:13.390
No!

09:13.390 --> 09:14.560
Why not?!

09:14.560 --> 09:16.020
I don't take students.

09:16.440 --> 09:17.860
And besides, we're in the middle of a trip!

09:17.860 --> 09:19.690
Please, accept us as your students!

09:19.690 --> 09:21.900
God, you're so persistent!

09:21.900 --> 09:23.360
Do you even have permission from your parents?!

09:23.360 --> 09:26.240
The thing is... those boys don't have any parents.

09:32.290 --> 09:34.210
I'm so soft when it comes to things like this...

09:43.670 --> 09:45.260
Survive on your own!

09:45.430 --> 09:46.430
Huh?

09:46.970 --> 09:48.300
That's the preliminary round.

09:48.800 --> 09:50.640
If you pass, we'll get to the real training.

09:51.100 --> 09:54.430
And you're not allowed to use alchemy during this preliminary round.

09:54.810 --> 09:55.690
What?

09:56.270 --> 09:58.560
"One is All, All is One."

09:58.940 --> 10:01.320
Find the answer to that within a month.

10:02.070 --> 10:05.990
If you can't, I'm sending you back to Resembool.

10:08.950 --> 10:09.740
Later!

10:12.080 --> 10:13.870
Huh?!

10:13.870 --> 10:17.170
What the heck?!

10:21.340 --> 10:23.710
So hungry...

10:23.710 --> 10:26.010
I want to sleep in a bed, geez...

10:33.100 --> 10:36.020
What part of this is alchemy training?!

10:40.560 --> 10:43.400
So hungry...

10:50.780 --> 10:52.870
I wonder if those kids are all right?

10:53.740 --> 10:56.410
They say there's no substitute for real-life experience.

10:56.910 --> 11:01.590
That is the best way to pound the courage portion of alchemy into them.

11:02.170 --> 11:07.170
If they don't learn anything from this,
it just means that's the extent of their talents.

11:07.760 --> 11:09.470
They'll have to give up learning from me.

11:12.720 --> 11:16.470
What I'm worried about is the safety of their lives.

11:16.680 --> 11:22.060
I was thrown out to Mt. Briggs in the middle of winter for a month during my training!

11:22.980 --> 11:25.730
Don't put yourself and ordinary people at the same level.

11:25.730 --> 11:29.740
There's so much to eat on that island; they'll live.

11:33.240 --> 11:34.620
We did it!

11:35.990 --> 11:38.120
How do we eat this?

11:38.120 --> 11:40.500
Hmm... We cut it apart.

11:40.500 --> 11:41.750
Cut it apart...

11:51.130 --> 11:52.300
I don't want to do it!

11:52.300 --> 11:53.760
You do it!

11:53.760 --> 11:55.850
I did the catching; you do the killing.

11:55.850 --> 11:58.180
You always try to make me do all the things you don't want to do!

12:03.900 --> 12:05.900
Get back here!!!

12:14.200 --> 12:15.740
Baby foxes...

12:19.450 --> 12:22.120
Forget meat... let's try for some fish.

12:26.040 --> 12:28.340
How do we catch one?!

12:28.340 --> 12:31.050
We don't have a rod, line, or a needle!

12:39.640 --> 12:44.020
No food, no fire, no nothing...

12:44.020 --> 12:45.400
Don't say that!

13:21.310 --> 13:21.980
Geez!

13:23.180 --> 13:25.190
What was that for, Brother?!

13:34.900 --> 13:36.110
Brother?

13:42.910 --> 13:44.210
Sour!

13:50.340 --> 13:52.710
I'm... alive.

13:54.300 --> 13:56.130
Eating ants and living.

14:02.810 --> 14:04.850
Eating life and living.

14:07.230 --> 14:08.230
Living...

14:11.610 --> 14:12.940
We're not going to die here!

14:12.940 --> 14:13.780
Right!

14:21.990 --> 14:23.290
Sorry about this...

14:29.250 --> 14:31.460
You're almost there, Brother.

14:38.180 --> 14:40.260
We did it!

15:01.160 --> 15:03.280
Looks like tomorrow's the end of the month...

15:04.290 --> 15:05.950
Hey Brother,

15:05.950 --> 15:09.870
did you ever find the answer to "One is All, All is One"?

15:12.040 --> 15:16.710
I've been thinking about it for the longest time, but I only kind of understand it.

15:17.550 --> 15:19.470
I'm not positive, but...

15:20.090 --> 15:24.220
Remember when I ate ants when we were starving and out of it?

15:24.390 --> 15:25.850
You did?

15:25.850 --> 15:27.770
Yep, I did.

15:27.770 --> 15:29.730
They were so sour.

15:29.980 --> 15:31.940
Then, a thought came to my mind.

15:32.400 --> 15:34.820
If I hadn't eaten them and eventually died,

15:34.820 --> 15:36.820
foxes and ants would eat me.

15:37.440 --> 15:39.530
I'd return to the soil and become grass.

15:39.990 --> 15:41.820
And that's what a rabbit would eat.

15:41.820 --> 15:43.620
The food chain, right?

15:43.620 --> 15:44.530
Yeah.

15:44.530 --> 15:45.740
But that's not all.

15:46.200 --> 15:50.540
Even this island could have been underwater in the ancient times.

15:50.540 --> 15:54.750
And tens of thousands of years in the future,
it could be a summit of a mountain.

15:54.750 --> 15:57.300
Everything is connected?

15:57.760 --> 16:02.090
Everything is within a large stream that can't be seen.

16:02.840 --> 16:06.760
I don't know if that stream should be called the universe or the world,

16:07.390 --> 16:12.150
but from the point of view of something that big, you and I are like ants.

16:12.980 --> 16:15.650
A small individual within a stream.

16:16.070 --> 16:18.360
We're just "one" within the "all".

16:18.940 --> 16:24.620
But only when those "ones" gather together, can an "all" exist.

16:31.250 --> 16:32.580
It's the promised day.

16:32.580 --> 16:36.040
Let's hear your answer to "One is All, All is One".

16:36.460 --> 16:37.960
"All" is the world!

16:37.960 --> 16:39.550
And "One" is me!

16:44.390 --> 16:46.550
Good! We can start the real training now.

16:47.640 --> 16:49.470
All right!

16:52.600 --> 16:55.610
A basis of a transmutation circle is the power of the circle.

16:55.610 --> 16:58.400
The circle displays the circulation of power,

16:58.400 --> 17:03.450
and by sketching the construction symbol in it,
it becomes possible to activate its power.

17:10.870 --> 17:12.750
This is also a circulation of power.

17:14.420 --> 17:16.210
It's best to experience it for yourself.

17:22.720 --> 17:23.840
Now...

17:23.840 --> 17:26.680
Review it until lunch is ready!

17:28.810 --> 17:30.180
Okay, so...

17:30.180 --> 17:32.850
The circle displays the circulation of power,

17:32.850 --> 17:38.480
and by sketching the construction symbol in it,
it becomes possible to activate its power.

17:39.650 --> 17:43.320
But you were transmuting by just slapping your palms together, weren't you, Master?

17:45.860 --> 17:48.070
Do you not need to sketch the construction symbols?

17:49.950 --> 17:53.080
I am like a construction symbol.

17:53.080 --> 17:55.000
What do you have to do in order to do that?

17:58.460 --> 18:02.010
You might be able to do it if you ever reach the truth.

18:07.640 --> 18:10.510
Master has also seen the truth...

18:20.690 --> 18:23.280
And? What did you want to talk to me about?

18:23.280 --> 18:24.570
W-Well...

18:39.500 --> 18:42.050
As I thought, you can transmute without a construction symbol!

18:44.090 --> 18:46.340
Additionally, Alphonse is an empty suit of armor!

18:46.340 --> 18:48.840
You've got automails for an arm and leg!

18:48.840 --> 18:50.470
How did you know, Master?!

18:50.470 --> 18:52.510
I can tell from just sparring with you!

18:54.430 --> 18:56.520
You... saw it, didn't you?

18:58.980 --> 19:00.150
Am I right?!

19:00.150 --> 19:01.440
Y-Yes, ma'am!

19:04.730 --> 19:07.030
Both master and pupil, making the same stupid decisions.

19:17.330 --> 19:18.500
Master, you...

19:19.250 --> 19:20.500
Because you saw that thing...

20:00.120 --> 20:03.880
We had a hard time conceiving a child.

20:05.420 --> 20:09.590
Just when we thought we were having a baby, I fell ill.

20:11.760 --> 20:16.180
Because of that, our child wasn't born into this world alive.

20:17.220 --> 20:18.270
So...

20:19.020 --> 20:20.520
...I committed taboo.

20:22.560 --> 20:25.360
Thanks to that, all sorts of organs were taken from me.

20:26.190 --> 20:27.980
I'm such an idiot.

20:33.910 --> 20:36.450
I should have told you sooner.

20:38.790 --> 20:39.910
It must have been tough.

20:42.750 --> 20:44.830
N-No!

20:44.830 --> 20:46.420
It's something we did to ourselves.

20:46.880 --> 20:48.920
We don't particularly find it tough...

20:48.920 --> 20:51.920
I think about what to eat when I get my body back.

20:51.920 --> 20:54.300
It's quite the opposite; it's more of an anticipation!

20:56.220 --> 20:57.560
Right, Brother?

20:57.560 --> 20:58.180
Yeah!

20:58.180 --> 20:59.600
That's exactly it!

20:59.600 --> 21:01.390
You morons...

21:06.480 --> 21:08.070
No need to force yourselves.

21:22.120 --> 21:23.620
Forgive us...

21:24.750 --> 21:25.880
We're sorry...

21:25.880 --> 21:26.630
Forgive us...

21:28.090 --> 21:28.880
We're sorry...

21:28.880 --> 21:29.670
Forgive us...

21:30.710 --> 21:31.760
We're sorry...

21:31.760 --> 21:32.880
Forgive us...

21:37.510 --> 21:42.770
This world is flowing while abiding by a great rule that's unimaginable.

21:43.180 --> 21:47.020
Learning about that flow,
breaking it down, and rebuilding it.

21:47.650 --> 21:49.520
That's what alchemy's all about.

21:49.900 --> 21:52.570
And it's also what living is about, too.

21:53.530 --> 21:57.820
The basics of alchemy, breaking
something down and rebuilding it...

21:57.820 --> 22:00.120
That's almost like the food chain.

22:00.120 --> 22:05.620
If you eat a rabbit, you break down
its meat and rebuild it into your own body.

22:06.040 --> 22:10.540
And even that rabbit rebuilds
the grass it ate into its own body.

22:11.340 --> 22:15.220
Alchemy is life itself.

22:27.590 --> 22:33.090
Say, the sky we saw that day, the scarlet sky.

22:27.590 --> 22:33.090
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora wo

22:33.090 --> 22:38.300
Do you remember it from that day?

22:33.090 --> 22:38.300
Nee kimi wa oboeteimasuka

22:38.300 --> 22:44.230
We made a promise and a vow while the early summer wind circled us.

22:38.300 --> 22:44.230
Yakusoku chigiri shoka no kaze ga tsutsumu

22:44.230 --> 22:48.480
And we clung close together.

22:44.230 --> 22:48.480
Futari yorisotta

22:52.030 --> 22:57.530
Your forced smile

22:52.030 --> 22:57.530
Muri na egao no ura

22:57.530 --> 23:02.910
Holds elongated shadows.

22:57.530 --> 23:02.910
Nobita kage wo kakumau

23:02.910 --> 23:12.170
I pretend not to notice and continue on.

23:02.910 --> 23:12.170
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei wo erabu

23:13.800 --> 23:21.680
All the while waiting for you to deliver some news at the table.

23:13.800 --> 23:21.680
Teeburu no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

23:24.310 --> 23:30.060
Empty nights, mornings that will never arrive,

23:24.310 --> 23:30.060
Kuuhaku no yoru mo kuru hazu no nai asa mo

23:30.060 --> 23:34.820
I could see them from a mile away.

23:30.060 --> 23:34.820
Zenbu wakattetanda

23:34.820 --> 23:40.450
Say, the sky we saw that day, the scarlet sky.

23:34.820 --> 23:40.450
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora wo

23:40.450 --> 23:45.370
I'm sure you'll remember it one day.

23:40.450 --> 23:45.370
Nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

23:45.370 --> 23:51.210
While holding the promise we couldn't keep,

23:45.370 --> 23:51.210
Hatasenakatta yakusoku wo idaite

23:51.210 --> 23:55.460
We take our first steps down our own paths.

23:51.210 --> 23:55.460
Futari arukidasu

23:59.170 --> 24:01.800
A man who enjoys his own desires.

